Replaces Dependabot #849, which bumped only `@fullcalendar/core` to 7.1.1 and left `@fullcalendar/angular`, `daygrid`, `interaction` and `timegrid` on ^6.1.20 (out of lockstep). #849 is left open for the user to close.

## Compatibility

`@fullcalendar/angular@7.1.1` peer-requires `@angular/core` / `@angular/common` **"16 - 22"** (npm metadata, also true of 7.0.0 to 7.1.0), so Angular 22.2 is supported. The upgrade guide still says 16-21; the published peer range is the authority.

## Packages

v7 restructured the family: `@fullcalendar/core` became `fullcalendar`, and `daygrid` / `timegrid` / `interaction` are no longer packages (their last stable is 6.1.21; v7 only shipped them as betas). They are entrypoints of the wrapper now.

| Before | After |
|---|---|
| `@fullcalendar/angular` ^6.1.20 | `@fullcalendar/angular` **7.1.1** (exact) |
| `@fullcalendar/core` ^6.1.20 | `fullcalendar` **7.1.1** (exact; brings `@fullcalendar/core` 7.1.1, preact 10.29.8) |
| `@fullcalendar/daygrid` / `interaction` / `timegrid` ^6.1.20 | removed: `@fullcalendar/angular/{daygrid,interaction,timegrid}` |
| | `temporal-polyfill` ^1.0.5 (new required peer, used as a ponyfill) |

Both FullCalendar packages are pinned exactly because the wrapper peer-requires `fullcalendar` at the exact same version. `.github/dependabot.yml` gets a `fullcalendar` group (`@fullcalendar/*`, `fullcalendar`, `temporal-polyfill`) so the family moves as one PR, like the `angular` group. Those packages are also excluded from `portal-minor-and-patch`, as `zone.js` is.

## Breaking changes and handling

- **Plugin imports**: moved to the `@fullcalendar/angular/*` entrypoints.
- **Types**: `CalendarOptions` / `EventInput` come from `@fullcalendar/angular`; `EventClickArg` became `EventClickInfo`; `DateClickArg` (was in the interaction plugin) became `DateClickInfo` (public API). The fields used here (`event.id`, `date`, `start`/`end` as `Date`) are unchanged.
- **CSS no longer bundled**: v7 needs `skeleton.css`, a theme stylesheet and the theme plugin. The calendar uses the **classic** theme (the v6 look). The stylesheets are loaded from the calendar component's own stylesheet, not angular.json's global styles, so they still ship only in the lazy `/appointments/calendar` chunk. The global `styles.css` is unchanged. The component is `ViewEncapsulation.None` because Preact creates FullCalendar's DOM outside Angular's renderer. Every rule of ours is scoped under `.cal-page`.
- **Theming via tokens**: v7 class names are hashed, and the `--fc-classic-*` variables are the supported hook. The stock `palette.css` (hard-coded `#3788d8` blue and slate buttons) is **not** loaded. The variables map onto `--primary`, `--primary-dark`, `--primary-light`, `--primary-tint`, `--primary-soft`, `--text-primary`, `--text-secondary` and `--border`, and the neutral fills are `color-mix` tints of `--text-primary`. They sit on `:root` in the lazy component stylesheet, because FullCalendar portals its "+N more" popover into `document.body`; the global styles bundle is byte-identical. The focus ring uses `--primary` (5.10:1), and the selection highlight is a translucent mix. Each `color-mix()` has a plain fallback in front of an `@supports` block, as FullCalendar's own `theme.css` does. Where the portal has no token, the colour is a named literal and is not given an invented fallback: white for text on primary, and `#b00020` for the error red. The provider `<select>` border meets 3:1.
- **Active view tab**: the theme distinguished it only by `--primary-dark` against `--primary`, about 1.5:1. It now inverts to a white fill with primary text and border, 5.10:1 against its neighbours, so it meets WCAG 1.4.11. It is selected by `[role=tab][aria-selected=true]`, because the theme's class names are hashed.
- **Locale**: the calendar follows the portal language from the same source as `LOCALE_ID` (`storedLang()`): French, Spanish, or the built-in English.
  - Only the language in use is downloaded, through a dynamic `import()`. The French chunk is 339 B and the Spanish one 636 B.
  - The calendar does not render until its locale has loaded, so it never shows English first. If a locale chunk fails to load, the calendar falls back to English rather than not appearing.
  - The locales are imported from `fullcalendar/locales/*` because the wrapper's `@fullcalendar/angular/locales/*` export is broken in 7.1.1: its export map points at `.mjs` files the package does not ship.
- `headerToolbar` is off by default in v7. It was already set explicitly here.
- The options used here are not among v7's renamed or removed ones (`eventClassNames`, `slotLabelFormat`, `buttonText`, `customButtons`, `updateSize`, `windowResize`, ...).
- **One fetch path**: `events` is now a function source, so FullCalendar requests every range it needs itself. In v6 the provider filter never refetched, because it waited for a `datesSet` that never came.
  - **The grid is never stale (privacy).** Picking a provider empties the grid first (`removeAllEvents`), then calls `refetchEvents()`. Every failed fetch also empties it, through `eventSourceFailure`. So another provider's patients never show under the new filter, even when the fetch fails.
  - **Retrying after an error:** `lazyFetching` is off. With it on, FullCalendar counts a failed range as already fetched, so switching from Week to Day never retried. Every view change now fetches, which also keeps a live schedule fresh.
  - **Retry button:** the error banner has one, which calls `refetchEvents()`. It reuses `COMMON.RETRY`, whose Spanish value was still the English "Retry" (47 uses); it is now "Reintentar".
  - **Error detail:** an HTTP error reaches FullCalendar as an `Error` that keeps the server's message and the original response as its `cause`. Before, it arrived as `[object Object]`.
- **Month-cell click**: an all-day cell now passes only `date`, no `time=00:00`.
- **Pre-fill (coordinator's decision, round 3):** `/appointments/new` reads neither query param, so pre-fill was never implemented. The form side stays out of this PR: the specs assert only the navigation parameters, and `tasklist.md` has a Standing platform debt bullet for it.
- v7 renders the view switcher as a tablist (`role="tab"`). Nothing in the portal or e2e selects those controls by role.

## Verification

- `lint`, `format:check`, `i18n:parity`, `i18n:referenced`, `build`, `test:coverage` (**Karma 2496/0**), `coverage:check`, `test:scripts` (98/0) all green locally.
- Specs render the real calendar in Karma and check:
  - the toolbar buttons resolve to `--primary`;
  - a probe in `<body>` sees the theme tokens;
  - the focus outline is `--primary`, and the highlight is translucent;
